+`tt=1` runs a one-way search even when `r` is set, and the results then say the fares are for a one-way trip. `tt=0` without `r` stays a round-trip search with an empty return date, so a one-way search needs `tt=1`.
+
 Airports are IATA codes only. City names get coerced to a "no flights" state, so resolve them from a static IATA table first;
  `/api/airports/lookup/search` returns 404. Dates must be `YYYY-MM-DD`, not in the past, and within United's 11 month window. Optional `noflex=true` disables the flexible date calendar above the grid. `tt=2` needs a different `f1`/`t1`/`d1` layout and is out of scope.
 
